  "body": "Related to #713 \r\n\r\nMigrate all examples to use WebGPUPathtracer, removing all WebGLPathtracer references - this should make it easier to see which examples are and aren't working and work towards getting the remaining features in. I've also fixed path tracer so it works without calling \"useMegakernel( bool )\" and defaulted it to use the wavefront mode.\r\n\r\nA number of the examples work quite well but I'm seeing some big performance drops in particular with the M2020 rover model in the \"viewer\" example (slower than the WebGL version). It's not clear to me why, yet.\r\n\r\n**Other**\r\n- Add webgpu-version BlurredEnvMapGenerator\r\n- Add support for \"stableNoise\", \"pause\" fields\r\n- Fix SkinnedMesh bounds\r\n- Adjust the default to use the wave front pathtracer\r\n- Fix support for Orthographic cameras\r\n\r\n**TODO**\r\n- Fix the remaining examples (or decide to punt)\r\n  - Fog (punt)\r\n  - Graphing (punt)\r\n  - AO Render (punt)\r\n  - LKG (delete / punt)\r\n  - Render Video (delete / punt)\r\n  - webgpu_primitives (delete?)\r\n\r\n**Later**\r\n- TLAS / BVH strategy for performance and adjusted getShapecastFn API\r\n- \"Stalenhag Winter\", Rover models are slow.\r\n  - Likely due to large TLAS overlap.\r\n- Lego models are slower when _not_ merging them.\r\n  - Visuals of the cockpit window change when merging the models for some reason?\r\n- Simplify redundancy between \"getBVH\" and BVH generation logic in WebGPUPathTracer.\r\n",
